{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/connectivity\/graphprotocols\/directedgraph\/nontrivialstronglyconnectedcomponents()"]}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/nontrivialStronglyConnectedComponents()","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"nontrivialStronglyConnectedComponents"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> ["},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:s10ArraySliceV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"ArraySlice"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P6VertexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":">]"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Tarjan’s algorithm, one pass: a self-loop is noticed while the search reads the vertex’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"successors."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The components are those of "},{"code":"stronglyConnectedComponents()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" without the trivial ones, in the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"same order, a reverse topological order: every path between two of them goes from a later"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one to an earlier one. Each lists its vertices in "},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" order. Empty exactly when the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"graph is acyclic. Each is a slice of one shared array, as in "},{"code":"attractingComponents()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", so its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"indices do not start at 0."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Each component’s first vertex is its earliest in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"text":", so one sort by that vertex’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"position puts the components in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"text":" order, O(C log C) for C components. On a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"StableDirectedGraph"},{"text":", where positions are insertion order:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let inInsertionOrder = graph.nontrivialStronglyConnectedComponents()","    .sorted { graph.vertexPosition(of: $0.first!) < graph.vertexPosition(of: $1.first!) }"],"type":"codeListing"},{"style":"note","name":"Complexity","type":"aside","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"O(V + E).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"metadata":{"title":"nontrivialStronglyConnectedComponents()","extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Connectivity\/NontrivialStronglyConnectedComponents.swift#L89","fileName":"NontrivialStronglyConnectedComponents.swift"},"externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P12ConnectivityE37nontrivialStronglyConnectedComponentsSays10ArraySliceVy6VertexQzGGyF","symbolKind":"method","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"nontrivialStronglyConnectedComponents"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s10ArraySliceV","text":"ArraySlice"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P6VertexQa","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":">]"}],"roleHeading":"Instance Method","modules":[{"relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"],"name":"Connectivity"}],"role":"symbol"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The nontrivial strongly connected components: the ones that contain a cycle, which are the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"components of two or more vertices and the single vertices with a self-loop. A vertex is in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one exactly when it lies on a cycle, and two vertices share one exactly when a cycle passes"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"through both."}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity","doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph"]]},"references":{"doc://Connectivity/documentation/Connectivity/GraphProtocols/DirectedGraph":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"DirectedGraph"}],"url":"\/documentation\/connectivity\/graphprotocols\/directedgraph","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"extension"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"DirectedGraph","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P"}],"title":"DirectedGraph","kind":"symbol","abstract":[]},"doc://Connectivity/documentation/Connectivity":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/connectivity","role":"collection","title":"Connectivity","kind":"symbol","abstract":[]},"doc://Connectivity/documentation/Connectivity/GraphProtocols":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/connectivity\/graphprotocols","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/GraphProtocols